  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nThe key insight is that the optimal h should exhibit a nested or wave-like structure where shifted versions minimize overlap. Traditional symmetric or clustered approaches may get stuck in local optima. This uses a physics-inspired optimization (swarm-particle jumps) and adaptive grid resolution to explore phase relations. We focus on sampling branch directions more effectively while validating solutions numerically.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\nThe step function h is represented as a piecewise constant function with discontinuities determined by an adaptive scale factor \u03b2. The optimization search samples shifts k directly within [-d,d] (d=2) and only evaluates viable k candidates (those exhibiting potential overlap-reducing structure). For F in [-1,1] (function value threshold), we enforce:\n   \u2200k: \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx \u2264 C and (1-|\u222bh-hShift|) \u2265 \u03b1P \nrepresented in continuous terms but validated discretely.\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n- Start with parent grid conversion to initial state s0\n- Use adaptive simulated annealing with entropic sorting:\n  1) Generate random phase shifts and length perturbations\n  2) Evaluate candidates via:\n      g(x) = discretized_overlap(x) \n      = max_k [sum_h(h[i]*(1-h[i+k]))/N ]\n  3) Maintain Pareto front between phase continuity and energy distribution\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\nOverlap thresholds T are dynamically adjusted:\n- If g_n / T_max < 0.0001 => tighten T_max\n- New phases triggered by gradient descent steps:\n  \u03b4p = argmax_{p}(SSE(p)),\u03b4n = argmin_{n}(SSE(n)) \nUse 2-Gaussian prior push sampling for interval centers: multi=2.0/len(grid)\n\n5. Resource budget and robustness:\n- Assumed grid size N=2048 (256 initial) \u00f7 (2*log(BUDGET_S))+256\n- Dynamic resolution adjustment: N = N*2 if no improvement & time>70%\n- Random projection fallback: if stuck, convert current state to grid using:\n  h_grid = np.zeros(N)\n  for each interval: h_grid[clip_idx]=1\n\n6. Validation contract:\nFinal solution must satisfy:\n\u222bh_grid = 1 0<=h_grid<=1\ncompute_c5(h_grid) <= C_bound + 0.00001\nOutput via: (best_grid, computed_bound, grid_size)",
